 * {{Symbol|Attack Modifier}}
** Jinada is an active attack modifier, and has the following properties:
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|[[Cast Range|CastRange]] {{=}} Hero[[Attack Range|AtkRange]]}}
*** Affected by {{M|attack range}} sources of the same range-type as the caster.
** Both {{M|Autocast}} and an active cast uses Gondar's current {{M|attack range}}.
*** Has Autocast on by default.
*** Fully functional while affected by {{M|silence}} sources, if set to {{M|Autocast}}.
** {{Symbol|Attack Damage|Instant}}
*** This ability component can be applied by other [[instant attack]] sources.

* {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
** The {{M|unreliable gold|x}} change component only affects enemy heroes.
*** Considers {{M|clones}} as heroes, {{M|illusions}} and {{M|creep-heroes}} as creeps.
** Does not affect the following units:
*** {{M|Buildings}}
*** {{M|Ward-type units}}.
** When attacking the aformentioned units, only the flat {{M|bonus attack damage|x}} component is applied, then procs the ability {{M|cooldown}}.

* {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}}
** All ability components do not affect allied units.

* {{Symbol|Cooldown}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
** Checks the ability's [[cooldown]] upon Gondar's {{M|attack point}}.
*** Jinada does not apply on the attack when its cooldown finishes during the {{M|attack animation}}.
** Grants flat {{M|bonus attack damage}} while off-cooldown, removing the bonus when going on cooldown.
** Grants Gondar exactly how much {{M|unreliable gold}} the affected target loses.

